# fstab — Orange Pi Zero 2W (Allwinner H618, arm64) headless appliance.
#
# This board is microSD-only for the installed root (no eMMC, no NVMe/PCIe at
# all on this SoC tier — see specs-orangepi-zero2w/README.md's storage confidence
# notes). Like the Frite/Orange-Pi-5 builders, this image produces LIVE/
# INSTALLER ISO media + a stage4 tarball — there is NO build_img/.img assembly
# step here. The LIVE flavor boots a squashfs root ephemerally (this fstab is
# largely inert there; / is the live overlay). The INSTALLER flavor
# (install-orangepi-zero2w.sh) partitions the target medium AT INSTALL TIME and
# rewrites the LABEL=/PARTUUID device columns below for the medium it actually
# wrote, so the installed system mounts the right partitions. The placeholder
# device paths below are replaced at install time; do not rely on them literally.
#
# <device>              <mount>  <type>   <options>                              <dump> <pass>
LABEL=OPIZ2W_BOOT     /boot    vfat     defaults,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec   0      2
LABEL=OPIZ2W_ROOT     /        ext4     defaults,noatime                       0      1
tmpfs                /tmp     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=128m 0      0
tmpfs                /run     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,mode=0755        0      0

# zram swap: this is a small, cheap appliance board (1GB/1.5GB/2GB/4GB LPDDR4
# RAM SKUs, RAM auto-detected — see the README); a zram helper is configured at
# first boot by the builder (mirrors La Frite's small-RAM SKU handling) rather than
# baked as a fixed swap partition here, since the SAME image runs across every
# RAM SKU.
